                  %a{:href => "#fully_faithful_essentially_surjective_functors"} Fully faithful essentially surjective functors
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#remarks"} Remarks
              %li
                %a{:href => "#adjoint_equivalence"} Adjoint equivalence
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#an_example_of_a_nonadjoint_equivalence"} An example of a non-adjoint equivalence
              %li
                %a{:href => "#in_higher_categories"} In higher categories
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The concept of
            %em equivalence of categories
            is the correct
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theoretic
            notion of “sameness” of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
          %p
            Concretely, an equivalence between two categories is a pair of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            between them which are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverse
            to each other
            %em up to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            of functors (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+functors"}> inverse functors
            ).
          %p
            This is like an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            of all categories. Hence abstractly an equivalence of categories is just the special case of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+a+2-category"} equivalence in a 2-category
            specialized to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
          %p
            If some foundational fine print is taken care of, then a functor exhibits an equivalence of categories precisely if it is both
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            is assumed. It remains true non-classically, say for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+categories"} internal categories
            = succeed "\u201D)," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctors"} anafunctors
            = succeed "\u201D)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+essentially+surjective"} split essentially surjective
          %p
            From the point of view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logic"} logic
            one may say that two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            are
            %em equivalent
            if they have the same
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/properties"} properties
            — although this only applies (by definition) to properties that obey the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+equivalence"} principle of equivalence
          %p
            Just as equivalence of categories is the generalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            from sets to categories, so the concept generalizes further to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher categories
            (see e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+2-categories"} equivalence of 2-categories
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-category"} categories
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          #EquivalenceViaInverseFunctor.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              An
              %strong equivalence
              between two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+a+2-category"} equivalence in the 2-category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              of all
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+functors"} inverse functors
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a pair of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %munderover
                          %mrow
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AA
                              %mi F
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AA
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟵
                            %mrow
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AA
                              %mi G
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AA
                        %mi 𝒟
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\mathcal{C}
                        \\underoverset
                        {\underset{\phantom{AA}F \phantom{AA}}{\longrightarrow}}
                        {\overset{\phantom{AA}G\phantom{AA}}{\longleftarrow}}
                        {}
                        \\mathcal{D},
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi G
                        %mo ≅
                        %msub
                          %mi Id
                          %mi 𝒟
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        F \circ G \cong Id_{\mathcal{D}}
                %p and
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi F
                        %mo ≅
                        %msub
                          %mi Id
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        G \circ F \cong Id_{\mathcal{C}}
                        \\,.
            %p
              This is called an
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+equivalence"} adjoint equivalence
              if the natural isomorphisms above satisfy the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+identities"} triangle identities
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              as a pair of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            %p
              Two categories are called
              %strong equivalent
              if there exists an equivalence between them.
          #ViaSplitEssentiallySurjectiveAndFullyFaithful.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  is part of an equivalence of categories in the sense of def.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivalenceViaInverseFunctor"}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  is
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      a
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+essentially+surjective+functor"} split essentially surjective functor
                      and
                  %li
                    %p
                      a
                      = succeed "." do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful functor
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              This proof is from the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+book"} HoTT book
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+categories"} univalent categories
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is an equivalence of categories with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi η
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G,\eta,\epsilon
              specified. Then we have the function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi hom
                              %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mi a
                            %mo ,
                            %mi F
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                            %msub
                              %mi hom
                              %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo ,
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                            %msubsup
                              %mi η
                              %mi b
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∘
                            %msub
                              %mi η
                              %mi a
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    hom_B(F a, F b) &amp;\to hom_A(a,b), \\
                    g &amp;\mapsto \eta_b^{-1}\circ G(g) \circ \eta_a.
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi hom
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:hom_A(a,b)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi η
                      %mi b
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi η
                      %mi b
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi b
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_b^{-1} \circ G(F(f)) \circ \eta_a = \eta_b^{-1} \circ \eta_b \circ f = f
            %p
              while for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi hom
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: hom_B(F a, F b)
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msubsup
                              %mi η
                              %mi b
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∘
                            %msub
                              %mi η
                              %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msubsup
                              %mi η
                              %mi b
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi η
                              %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi ϵ
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mi b
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi η
                              %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi g
                            %mo ∘
                            %msub
                              %mi ϵ
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mi a
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi η
                              %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    F(\eta_b^{-1} \circ G(g) \circ \eta_a) &amp;= F(\eta_b^{-1}) \circ F(G(g)) \circ F(\eta_a) \\
                    \&amp;= \epsilon_{F b} \circ F(G(g)) \circ F(\eta_a) \\
                    \&amp;= g \circ \epsilon_{F a} \circ F(\eta_a) \\
                    \&amp;= g
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              using
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturality
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{a,b}
              is an equivalence, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful"} fully faithful
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G b : A
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi F
                      %mi G
                      %mi b
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon_b : F G b \cong b
            %p
              On the other hand, suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful"} fully faithful
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+essentially+surjective"} split essentially surjective
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_0:B_0\to A_0
              by sending
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:B
              to the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
              given by the specified essential splitting, and write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon_b
              for the likewise specified
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mi G
                      %mi b
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F G b \cong b
            %p
              Now for any
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi hom
                        %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: hom_B(b,b')
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi hom
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(g): hom_A(G b, G b')
              to be the unique morphism such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
