          %h2#Variants Variants
          %p
            We discuss some possible variants of the definition of equivalence of categories, each of which comes naturally from a different view of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
          %p
            The first,
            = succeed "," do
              %em isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            as a mere
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+categories"} strict categories
            = succeed "," do
              %em strong equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            as a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"} strict 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            holds. The next definition,
            = succeed "," do
              %em weak equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            as a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            = succeed "," do
              %em anaequivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            that is not (without the axiom of choice) equivalent (as a bicategory!) to the strict
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
          %p
            It is also possible to define ‘category’ in such a way that only a correct definition can be stated, but here we use the usual algebraic definitions of category,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
          %h3#Isomorphism Isomorphism
          %p
            Two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+categories"} strict categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            are
            %strong isomorphic
            if there exist
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+functors"} strict functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
